#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# NexusBackup diagnostics: self-checks and redacted support bundles (Phase 14b).
#
#   nexus-diag tick     what nexus-diag.service runs (nexus-diag.path, PathExists=request.json):
#                       handle pending requests, prune results older than 24 h
#   nexus-diag checks   print the checks as JSON (nexus-update runs this before it stages or
#                       applies an update; an admin on the console can run it as well)
#
# Control directory (default /var/lib/nexus/diag, 2770 root:nexus-webapi, see
# tmpfiles.d/nexus-diag.conf) is the interface for the web-api:
#   request.json   written by the web-api (tmp + rename), at most 4 KiB:
#                  {"id": <32 hex>, "kind": "checks"|"bundle", "by": <user>, "since": <unix>, "until": <unix>}
#                  consumed (deleted) by the next tick, which nexus-diag.path starts at once
#   <id>/status.json  {"id", "kind", "by", "created", "since", "until", "state": running|done|error,
#                  "error", "files": {"checks.json": bytes, "bundle.tar.gz": bytes}}
#   <id>/checks.json  the checks (both kinds)
#   <id>/bundle.tar.gz  the support bundle (kind "bundle"): see BUNDLE below
#
# Checks: {id, title, status pass|warn|fail|skip, severity 1-4, detail, manual}. severity:
# 1 info, 2 warning, 3 error, 4 critical. nexus-update refuses to stage or apply an update
# while a check with severity >= 3 fails. "manual" is the anchor in the user manual.
#
# Redaction (redact() below, tests in os/greenboot/tests/test_nexus_diag.py): every text
# file of the bundle passes through it. Removed: PEM blocks, Authorization / Cookie
# headers, bearer and API tokens, values of password/secret/token/key/seed/... fields,
# passwords in URLs, otpauth secrets, download tokens. Kept: host names and IP
# addresses (support needs them to follow connections and firewall drops), digests,
# audit hashes (not secret), user names.
#
# Runs as root in its own SELinux domain (nexus_diag_t): read-only access to the
# journal, audit log, nftables, chrony, systemd state, the catalog, the update status and
# the disk status of nexus-disks (it never opens a disk itself);
# writes only below the control directory; no network (IPAddressDeny=any, no inet
# sockets in the policy). Every path and tool can be overridden through NEXUS_DIAG_*
# environment variables (see DEFAULTS); the unit tests use that. Stdlib only.

